# AUTONOMOUS STATIONS - a starbase that runs its own wings.
#
# When nobody is there to give it orders - no crew on its side or an allied one - or it is
# marked `autonomous`, or a crew said "Act on your own", a station flies its wings itself.
# The POLICY is hangar_wing_think() in hangar_wing.py (one place, unit-tested); this file
# only carries its decisions out with the SAME objective labels a crew's orders use, so an
# autonomous wing and an ordered one fly identical code.
#
# A brain rather than a ticker, like the turrets: brains get the rolling slicer and die
# with their agent. The brain asks hangar_wing_is_autonomous every pass, so a station
# changes hands the moment a crew joins its side, or delegates it.


# Every station gets the brain; one with no bays (civil, skaraan, torgoth...) is skipped.
# The wait lets the players and sides exist first - the same reason hangar.mast waits.
//spawn if has_role(SPAWNED_ID, "station")
    await delay_sim(1)
    ->END if not object_exists(SPAWNED_ID)
    ->END if len(hangar_wing_names(SPAWNED_ID)) == 0
    brain_add(SPAWNED_ID, hangar_wing_command)


# A hit on a station is what launches its reserve wing.
//damage/object if has_role(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID, "station") and len(hangar_wing_names(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID)) > 0
    hangar_wing_note_attacked(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID, DAMAGE_PARENT_ID if DAMAGE_PARENT_ID else DAMAGE_ORIGIN_ID)


=== hangar_wing_command
" Station running its own fighter wings
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/station
```
    yield fail if not hangar_wing_is_autonomous(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    for wing_act, wing_key, wing_target in hangar_wing_think(BRAIN_AGENT_ID):
        if wing_act == "attack":
            for wing_id in hangar_wing_launch(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, None, wing_key):
                objective_add(wing_id, objective_attack_target, {"objective_target": wing_target, "objective_target_point": None})
        elif wing_act == "protect":
            for wing_id in hangar_wing_launch(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, None, wing_key):
                objective_add(wing_id, objective_escort, {"objective_target": wing_target, "objective_target_point": None})
        elif wing_act == "reassign":
            for wing_id in hangar_wing_reassign(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, wing_key):
                objective_clear(wing_id)
                objective_add(wing_id, objective_attack_target, {"objective_target": wing_target, "objective_target_point": None})
        elif wing_act == "recall":
            for wing_id in hangar_wing_out(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, wing_key):
                objective_clear(wing_id)
                objective_add(wing_id, hangar_wing_return)
    yield success


# DELEGATION - a crew hands a station to its own AI, or takes it back. `keeps_objective`:
# neither is a new job for the station, so carry_out_orders leaves its objective alone.
=== objective_wing_delegate
metadata: ```
display_name: Act on your own
type: objective/orders/launch/delegate
valid_for: self
requires: wing_delegable
keeps_objective: true
ack: Understood, running our own wings
```
    " Hand the station's wings to its own AI until a bridge gives it an order
    hangar_wing_delegate(OBJECTIVE_AGENT_ID, True)
    yield success


=== objective_wing_undelegate
metadata: ```
display_name: Await orders
type: objective/orders/launch/undelegate
valid_for: self
requires: wing_delegated
keeps_objective: true
ack: Standing by for orders
```
    " Take the station's wings back under the bridge's orders
    hangar_wing_delegate(OBJECTIVE_AGENT_ID, False)
    yield success
